        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f7a12d91b3f4f59840be80c62c87dd2",
      "statement": "Gemini accepts four authentication paths in priority order: (1) `GEMINI_API_KEY`, (2) `GOOGLE_API_KEY` + `GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true` (Vertex AI), (3) `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` (OAuth / Code Assist, requires interactive login), (4) default OAuth via the CLI prompt. `validateEnvironmentVariables` only enforces `GEMINI_API_KEY`, so the gate is more permissive than the wrapper itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/agents/gemini.ts#L178-L200",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd12433d18ed97603fee2fa5f3d17d5a6da8c66ae65443d64ca72b7a9209758a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/config.ts#L27-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02a89a550fd111b923f6b9e0b79522153f02f8c655c837fa79702d942b27b766:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_339d366b961542388a563e4a2c728d12",
      "statement": "OpenCode refuses to run if neither `OPENAI_API_KEY` nor `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set. For each key that is present, the wrapper pipes it into `opencode auth add PROVIDER` (so the OpenCode CLI stores it as its own credential) and additionally exports the key on the final shell invocation. The wrapper is the only one that registers credentials via the CLI's own `auth add` command rather than via config files or env-only injection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/agents/opencode.ts#L241-L283",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:147fd2173435affff67344bb3d4b2e12ada84cc2163dd2d45d885ef097c6aa67:"
